---
apiVersion: kuttl.dev/v1beta1
kind: TestStep
timeout: 300
commands:
  # Kill the agent's liveness signal. Scaling the Deployment to 0 is NOT enough on its own: the operator
  # manages the agent Deployment and re-applies replicas=1 on its next reconcile (~20s), and the fresh
  # pod renews the Lease inside the 30s staleness window — so `available` never flips. Instead, also
  # DELETE the Lease: is_agent_alive treats an absent Lease as not-alive, and the operator (which watches
  # the Lease) writes available=false almost immediately. The signal is transient — the resurrected agent
  # recreates the Lease in ~20-30s — so there is deliberately NO sleep here: the assert must start polling
  # at once to observe the window (kuttl passes on the first match).
  - script: kubectl scale deploy/test-kafka-kafka-agent --replicas=0 -n $NAMESPACE
  - script: kubectl delete lease test-kafka-kafka-agent -n $NAMESPACE --ignore-not-found
